Dockerfile
============================================================
FROM python:3.12-slim

WORKDIR /srv

COPY pyproject.toml ./
RUN pip install --no-cache-dir uv && uv pip install --system -r pyproject.toml

COPY app ./app

EXPOSE 8000
CMD ["uvicorn", "app.main:app", "--host", "0.0.0.0", "--port", "8000"]
============================================================
README.md
============================================================
# VideoPlatform

Generated by [CIaC](https://github.com/jrcalgo/ciac) — do not edit the
compiler-owned wiring by hand; regenerate it from the `.ciac` source
instead. Business logic lives in `app/services/`, which is yours.

## Run

```sh
uv sync
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

Workers run separately:

```sh
uv run python -m app.workers
```

Or bring up the full stack (API, workers, Postgres, Redis, NATS):

```sh
docker compose up --build
```

## Test & lint

```sh
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
```

## Layout

| Path | Purpose | Owner |
|------|---------|-------|
| `app/main.py` | Application assembly | compiler |
| `app/api/` | HTTP routers (one per api) | compiler |
| `app/services/` | Business-logic handlers | **you** |
| `app/workers/` | Queue consumers | compiler |
| `app/config.py` | Environment-driven settings | compiler |

Requests to protected routes need a bearer token signed with
`JWT_SECRET` (default `change-me`, algorithm HS256).
